 "manufacturer": "Vishay Semiconductors",
 "title": "TEPT4400: ambient light sensor, silicon NPN phototransistor in a 3 mm T-1 leaded package",
 "source": {
  "document": "Document Number 81341",
  "revision": "Rev. 1.8, 30-Jun-16",
  "pages": 5
 },
 "summary": "A silicon NPN epitaxial planar phototransistor whose response follows the human eye, peaking at 570 nm and spanning 440 to 800 nm at half response, in a 3 mm (T-1) through-hole body with two leads, emitter and collector. At 100 lx of CIE illuminant A and VCE = 5 V it passes 200 µA typ; at 20 lx the photocurrent lies between 15 and 70 µA and parts ship sorted into three bins (A, B, C) inside that range. Half-sensitivity angle is ±30°. Intended uses are display backlight dimming and keypad lighting control in LCDs and handheld devices, on/off lighting control in industry, and replacing CdS photocells.",
